"\n"
"This module addresses the two main tax requirements in Thailand.\n"
"\n"
"1. Tax Invoice (VAT)\n"
"--------------------\n"
"\n"
"The point of tax invoice can occur either on the invoice (VAT) or on the\n"
"payment (undue VAT, which becomes VAT on payment).\n"
"\n"
"- Tax invoices are recorded on journal entries and listed in Accounting\n"
"  > Accounting > Tax Invoices, the source of the Thai VAT report.\n"
"- The number and date of a purchase tax invoice are filled in from the\n"
"  vendor's tax invoice, sales tax invoices are numbered when posting.\n"
"- They replace the sales tax invoices of the standard ``l10n_th``\n"
"  module, which are not created, and its ``VAT Registered`` option is\n"
"  hidden.\n"
"\n"
"2. Withholding Tax and Personal Income Tax\n"
"------------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"It is built on the standard ``l10n_th`` and\n"
"``l10n_account_withholding_tax`` modules, for Thai companies only. The\n"
"withholding tax is deducted during the payment, with two kinds of\n"
"calculation.\n"
"\n"
"1. Fixed rate of the base amount, e.g., service 3%\n"
"2. Progressive rate of the yearly accumulated income, i.e., personal\n"
"   income tax (PIT)\n"
"\n"
"Withholding tax certificates, PND forms and the withholding tax and PIT\n"
"reports are provided on top of it.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Withholding Tax\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"Withholding taxes are standard taxes, there is no specific master data.\n"
"\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Configuration > Accounting > Taxes and create a tax\n"
"  with ``Is Withholding Tax`` checked and a negative rate, e.g., -3% for\n"
"  a service\n"
"- Set the withholding tax payable account on its tax repartition\n"
"- Set the standard ``Income Tax Type`` of the tax, it is the default\n"
"  type of income on the withholding tax certificate\n"
"- Optionally, set a PND tax tag on the repartition lines of the tax,\n"
"  e.g., ``PND53`` or ``Income PND53``, as the standard 50 Tawi report.\n"
"  It is the default PND form of the certificate, otherwise PND53 for\n"
"  companies and PND3 for individuals. Tags for PND3 and PND53 are\n"
"  standard, this module adds PND1, PND2 and PND3a.\n"
"\n"
"Go to Accounting > Configuration > Settings and select the\n"
"``Withholding Tax Base`` account. It is used by the ``WH Base`` and\n"
"``Counterpart`` lines of the payments with withholding tax.\n"
"\n"
"To print the payer signature on the 50 Tawi, go to Accounting >\n"
"Configuration > Settings > Thai Localization and check\n"
"``50 Tawi - Print Signature``. The name of the user who confirmed the\n"
"certificate is printed above the signature line.\n"
"\n"
"The codes of the income types, used on the certificates, are available\n"
"in Accounting > Configuration > Accounting > WHT Income Code.\n"
"\n"
"Personal Income Tax (PIT)\n"
"-------------------------\n"
"\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Configuration > Accounting > Taxes and create the\n"
"  PIT tax as a withholding tax, then check ``Personal Income Tax``. The\n"
"  rate is fixed to 0% (the amount is hidden), the amount to withhold is\n"
"  computed on the payment. There can be only one PIT tax per company.\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Configuration > Accounting > PIT Rate to review the\n"
"  rate tables. There is one table per calendar year, the default rates\n"
"  in effect since 2017 are provided. Create a new table when the rates\n"
"  change.\n"
"\n"
"Tax Invoices\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"**Preparing Undue Tax**\n"
"\n"
"- Use Developer Mode\n"
"- In Chart of Accounts, add a new account for Undue Tax, if it does not\n"
"  already exist.\n"
"- As admin, add the access right ``Show Full Accounting Features``\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Configuration > Settings and select ``Cash Basis``,\n"
"  this will open the cash basis options in the Tax master data\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Configuration > Accounting > Taxes, create new\n"
"  undue taxes for both sales and purchase\n"
"\n"
"**Sales Tax Invoice Number**\n"
"\n"
"The sales tax invoice is numbered when the entry is posted.\n"
"\n"
"- For sales taxes (tax scope = Sales), choose the\n"
"  ``Tax Invoice Sequence`` (or create a new one) to number the tax\n"
"  invoice by sequence. Set the same sequence for the same tax on\n"
"  payment, i.e., Output VAT7% and Undue Output VAT7% must select the\n"
"  same sequence, so that both result in the same tax report.\n"
"- Otherwise, the tax invoice number is the number of the invoice. For\n"
"  undue VAT, go to Accounting > Configuration > Settings > Thai\n"
"  Localization and select the ``Customer Tax Invoice Number``, either\n"
"  the payment number or the invoice number.\n"
"\n"
"Note: these options are not available for purchase taxes, because the\n"
"tax invoice number is from the vendor and filled in manually.\n"
"\n"
"**Keep Zero Line Taxes**\n"
"\n"
"To keep tax lines with zero amount (such as 0% VAT) in journal entries,\n"
"so that they appear in the tax invoices:\n"
"\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Configuration > Settings and select\n"
"  ``Keep Zero Line Taxes``\n"
"- Create an invoice or bill and select a tax with 0% rate\n"
"- Go to Journal Items, a tax line with zero value is created\n"
"\n"
"Zero withholding tax lines are never kept.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Withholding Tax\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"**Vendor bills and customer invoices**\n"
"\n"
"- Create the bill or invoice and set the withholding tax in ``Taxes`` of\n"
"  the lines. Only one withholding tax is allowed per line.\n"
"- Post it, then click Pay (Register Payment)\n"
"- In the payment wizard, select ``Withhold`` (pay and withhold, or\n"
"  withhold only), the withholding lines are proposed from the taxes of\n"
"  the bill. Their base and amount can be edited.\n"
"- Create the payment. The amounts withheld are recorded on the payment\n"
"  with the ``WH Base`` and ``Counterpart`` lines.\n"
"\n"
"**Manual journal entries**\n"
"\n"
"Set the withholding tax in ``Taxes`` of a journal item. The withholding\n"
"tax line is computed directly on the entry.\n"
"\n"
"**Withholding tax certificates**\n"
"\n"
"- On a posted payment or journal entry with withholding tax, an alert\n"
"  tells that the certificate is not yet created. Click\n"
"  ``Create withholding tax cert.``\n"
"- The certificates are created per partner and PND form. The PND form\n"
"  defaults from the PND tax tags of the tax, otherwise from the partner,\n"
"  i.e., company: PND53, individual: PND3, and can be edited. The type of\n"
"  income defaults from the income tax type of the tax, and the tax payer\n"
"  from the withholding condition of the payment. Check the type of\n"
"  income and income code, then confirm the certificate.\n"
"- Certificates are listed in Accounting > Vendors > WHT Certificates.\n"
"- Print a done certificate with ``Print 50 Tawi``, the standard 50 Tawi\n"
"  report of ``l10n_th`` filled from the certificate. Several\n"
"  certificates are downloaded as a ZIP file with Action > Thailand:\n"
"  Print 50 tawi. These replace the standard ones of payments, which are\n"
"  hidden.\n"
"- Send the 50 Tawi of a done certificate to the partner with\n"
"  ``Send by Email``.\n"
"- Resetting to draft or cancelling the payment or journal entry also\n"
"  cancels its certificates.\n"
"\n"
"**Reports**\n"
"\n"
"Go to Accounting > Reporting > Thai Accounting Reports > Withholding Tax\n"
"\n"
"Personal Income Tax (PIT)\n"
"-------------------------\n"
"\n"
"- Set the PIT tax in ``Taxes`` of the bill lines, e.g., for freelancers.\n"
"  It is 0% on the bill.\n"
"- Click Pay and select ``Withhold``. The PIT is computed on the payment\n"
"  from the yearly income accumulated by the partner, with the PIT rate\n"
"  table of the payment year. The yearly income includes the base of the\n"
"  posted payments and journal entries of the partner.\n"
"- A certificate can be created from the payment as for any other\n"
"  withholding tax.\n"
"- Go to Accounting > Reporting > Thai Accounting Reports > Personal\n"
"  Income Tax to see the yearly income and the PIT withheld.\n"
"\n"
"Tax Invoice\n"
"-----------\n"
"\n"
"The tax invoice is recorded on each journal entry with VAT, in the\n"
"``Tax Invoice`` tab, and listed in Accounting > Accounting > Tax\n"
"Invoices. The fields are the tax invoice number and date, and the number\n"
"of months of late report.\n"
"\n"
"Note: the table ``account.move.tax.invoice`` is the main source of the\n"
"Thai VAT report.\n"
"\n"
"**Customer Invoice and Payment**\n"
"\n"
"- Create a customer invoice and choose the sales VAT or undue VAT\n"
"- Post the invoice and register the payment as usual. The tax invoice is\n"
"  numbered when posting, by the tax sequence, or by the invoice or\n"
"  payment number (see the configuration).\n"
"\n"
"**Vendor Bill with Input VAT**\n"
"\n"
"- Create a vendor bill and choose the Input VAT\n"
"- In the ``Tax Invoice`` tab, fill in ``Tax Invoice`` and ``Tax Date``\n"
"  given by your vendor. They are required before posting.\n"
"- Post the vendor bill, the tax invoice keeps the number and date.\n"
"\n"
"**Vendor Bill with Undue Input VAT**\n"
"\n"
"- Create a vendor bill and choose the Undue Input VAT, then post it\n"
"- Register the payment as usual\n"
"- The cash basis entry that clears the undue VAT is created, but it\n"
"  stays in **Draft** until the vendor's tax invoice is filled in\n"
"- In the ``Tax Invoice`` tab of the payment, fill in the Tax Invoice\n"
"  Number and Tax Date, then click ``Clear Tax``. The cash basis entry is\n"
"  **Posted** (or post the entry itself).\n"
"\n"
"Note: when a bill is netted with a refund or a journal entry, Odoo 20\n"
"does not create a cash basis entry.\n"
"\n"
"**Report Late**\n"
"\n"
"A vendor tax invoice dated in an earlier month than the accounting date\n"
"can be reported late, up to 6 months. ``Report Late`` is proposed when\n"
"the tax invoice date is filled in, and the report date is then moved to\n"
"the end of the later month.\n"
"\n"
"**Split**\n"
"\n"
"In draft, use the ``Split`` button on a line of the ``Tax Invoice`` tab\n"
"to copy it, when the vendor issues several tax invoices for the same\n"
"journal item. Adjust the tax base and tax amount of each one.\n"
"\n"
"**Credit Notes and Reversals**\n"
"\n"
"When reversing a vendor bill or entry, the reversal wizard asks for the\n"
"vendor credit note number and date. The tax invoice of the reversal has\n"
"a negative base and amount.\n"
"\n"
"**Manual Tax Invoice**\n"
"\n"
"On journal entries, check ``Manual Tax Invoice`` on a journal item\n"
"(e.g., a VAT account line without tax) to create its tax invoice, for\n"
"example, for a purchase VAT recorded manually.\n"
"\n"
"Changelog\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"20.0.1.0.0\n"
"----------\n"
"\n"
"**Breaking changes**\n"
"\n"
"- Rebuilt on top of the standard ``l10n_th`` and\n"
"  ``l10n_account_withholding_tax`` modules. The withholding taxes are\n"
"  standard taxes (``Is Withholding Tax``). Tax invoices and withholding\n"
"  tax certificates apply to Thai companies only.\n"
"- Removed the models ``account.withholding.tax`` and\n"
"  ``account.withholding.move``, the ``WHT Account`` flag on accounts,\n"
"  the withholding tax on products and ``wht_tax_id`` on journal items.\n"
"- The standard Thai tax invoices of ``l10n_th`` (``VAT Registered``) are\n"
"  not created, the tax invoices of this module are used instead.\n"
"- Removed the ``Default Type of Income`` of taxes, the type of income of\n"
"  the certificates defaults from the standard ``Income Tax Type``.\n"
"- There is no data migration from older versions.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/OCA/l10n-thailand/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/OCA/l10n-thailand/issues/new?body=module:%20l10n_th_account_tax%0Aversion:%2020.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
